  "knowledge": "Stellar Luminosity",
  "description": "Calculates a star's luminosity relative to the Sun using its temperature and radius.",
  "definition": "Luminosity ($L_{\\star}$) relative to the Sun is estimated using the Stefan-Boltzmann law: $L_{\\star} = \\left( \\frac{R_{\\star}}{R_{\\odot}} \\right)^2 \\left( \\frac{T_{\\star}}{T_{\\odot}} \\right)^4$, where $R_{\\star}$ is the star's radius, $T_{\\star}$ is its effective temperature, and $T_{\\odot}$ is the Sun's effective temperature (~5778 K)."
